## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a compliant, production-grade retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) assistant for contract processing. It evaluates understanding of multi-tenant security, data isolation, and regulatory compliance patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with Cognitive Search knowledge base
- Per-tenant isolation via Key Vault and customer-managed keys (CMK)
- PII redaction with consent-based access control
- Policy engine to detect and block sensitive prompt patterns
- End-to-end audit trail to Data Lake for compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode policy snippet
function isAllowed(prompt, piiPresent, consentGiven) {
  if (piiPresent && !consentGiven) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'PII detected without consent' };
  }
  if (containsSensitivePatterns(prompt)) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'Sensitive content blocked' };
  }
  return { allowed: true };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes governance at scale: per-tenant safety, data residency, and cost-aware routing in a live Azure OpenAI pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-aware policy packs in blob storage
- PDP (policy decision point) in Azure Functions
- Data residency routing to OpenAI regional endpoints
- Redaction and guardrails before outbound calls
- Auditing and observability via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePDP(tenantId, metadata, policies) {
  const policy = policies[tenantId] || policies["default"];
  // residency check
  if (policy.residency && policy.residency !== metadata.region) return { action: "block" };
  // budget constraint
  if (typeof policy.budget === "number" && metadata.cost > policy.budget) return { action: "redirect", destination: "onPrem" };
  // allowed destination
  if (policy.allowedDestinations?.includes("OpenAI")) return { action: "allow", destination: "OpenAI" };
  return { action: "block" };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test PDP edge cases (missing tenant, malformed metadata, policy drift)?
- How would you implement zero-downtime policy updates and per-tenant rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design governance-aware AI copilots that enforce enterprise privacy policies, implement policy-as-code, and ensure auditable, defensible decisions in multi-tenant environments.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI integration with API Management for secure API exposure
- Cognitive Search knowledge base grounding against versioned Azure Blob storage
- Policy-as-code modules for privacy, consent, and data retention enforcement
- Per-tenant Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) via Azure Active Directory
- Comprehensive auditable logging in Azure Data Lake or equivalent storage
- End-to-end test harness for validation across all components

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePolicy(request, kb, policy) {
  const redactedRequest = redactPII(request, policy.piiRules);
  const groundedContext = await searchKnowledgeBase(redactedRequest, kb);
  const consentCheck = validateConsent(redactedRequest, policy.consentRules);
  const retentionCheck = validateRetention(redactedRequest, policy.retentionRules);

  if (!consentCheck.valid || !retentionCheck.valid) {
    return { decision: 'DENY', rationale: [...consentCheck.reasons, ...retentionCheck.reasons] };
  }

  const decision = await openai.chat.completions.create({
    messages: [{ role: 'system', content: policy.determinationPrompt },
               { role: 'user', content: JSON.stringify({ request: redactedRequest, context: groundedContext }) }]
  });

  return parseDecision(decision);
}
```
